{
  "id": "top-k-frequent-elements",
  "questionId": "top-k-frequent-elements",
  "slug": "top-k-frequent-elements",
  "title": "Top K Frequent Elements",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Hash map",
  "patterns": [
    "hash map",
    "heap"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "sorting ALL distinct values by frequency does more work than necessary when you only need the top k. what structure keeps just the k best candidates without a full sort?",
    "a min-heap of size k works: push each (value, frequency), and whenever the heap exceeds size k, pop the smallest - what's left are the k largest",
    "alternatively, since frequency can't exceed the length of nums, you could bucket values by frequency (a list of buckets, index = frequency) and read off the top k from the highest-frequency buckets first, avoiding a heap entirely",
    "don't forget the tie-break rule - group your comparison so equal frequencies land in a well-defined order"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "sorting the full list of distinct values when only a k-sized heap or bucket pass was needed",
    "returning values in insertion or hash-iteration order instead of following the frequency-then-value ordering rule",
    "off-by-one when only keeping the heap at size k (popping too early or too late)"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array of integers `nums` and an integer `k`.\n\n**Return the `k` most frequent values.**\n\nTo keep the answer well-defined, order the result by frequency descending, and break ties by value ascending.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 10^5",
      "-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4",
      "1 <= k <= number of distinct values in nums"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "k equals the number of distinct values (return all of them)",
      "every value appears the same number of times (tie-break decides everything)",
      "a single distinct value repeated many times"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
